1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,820
One person clicks once: one request. Now fifty thousand people click the same profile.

2
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:11,320
All those requests reach the database. Connections and disk reads pile up.

3
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:17,620
The cache checks first. A miss reads the database, stores the profile, and responds.

4
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:23,300
A hit returns the profile from memory in about one point one milliseconds, not four.

5
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:29,740
TTL limits staleness. The database still matters. Stampedes need design.
